              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "12788229"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Occurs in almost all aerobically respiring organisms and serves to protect cells from the toxic effects of hydrogen peroxide. Its accumulation in prespore cells affords the spores protection from oxidation during prolonged dormancy. Required for normal developmental timing, possibly through a regulatory role in differentiation and morphogenesis"
        }
